## Error Handling

| Issue | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| Invalid [brain-file-name] format | Ensure [brain-file-name] uses kebab-case and ends with .md |
| [brain-file-name] already exists | Choose a different name or update existing file as appropriate |
| [brain-file-name] missing .md extension | Append .md to the filename |
| Invalid header format | Follow exact header template with all components in [brain-file-name] |
| Missing sections | Review parameter-template and add required sections to [brain-file-name] |
| Reference-format issues | Wrap @ symbols in backticks, use proper extensions |
| Integration problems | Verify file location and update related documentation |
| Pathway mismatch | Ensure pathway in header matches message-command |
| Component verification failures | Verify all 5 message-command components match parameter header |

## Message-Command Verification

The parameter verifies these components from the message-command:
1. **mode**: Must be "direct-mode"
2. **workflow-type**: Must be "rules-workflow"
3. **pathway-name**: Must be "none"
4. **project-rule-parameter**: Must be "@parameters/rules/direct-mode/add-project-rule-parameter.mdc"
5. **optional-standard-parameter(s)**: Must end with ".md" (this is the [brain-file-name] variable)

### Standard-Parameter Validation

The [brain-file-name] standard-parameter is validated with these rules:
- Must end with ".md" extension
- Should use kebab-case formatting (lowercase with hyphens)
- Should be descriptive of the parameter's purpose
- Should not contain spaces or special characters
- Should not already exist in the target location (unless updating is intended)

